<span class="tag" style="--tag:#F4C95D">Operations Automation</span>
<h2>Warehouse Order Preparation Tool</h2><p>A desktop application that converts Trendyol and Hepsiburada order exports into a clean, warehouse-ready Excel workbook.</p>
</div>
<div class="detail-grid">
<div class="detail-block"><h4>Problem</h4><p>Trendyol and Hepsiburada export their daily order lists in different formats. Trendyol includes an extra notice row and many unnecessary columns, while Hepsiburada arrives as CSV and sometimes provides seller stock codes as ENT-HB barcode values. Preparing the warehouse list required daily manual column cleanup, stock-code checks, and file merging.</p></div>
<div class="detail-block"><h4>Solution</h4><p>The tool accepts the Trendyol XLSX file, the Hepsiburada CSV file, and a barcode-to-stock-code database workbook from one screen. It removes the unnecessary Trendyol row, keeps only the required columns, cleans the Hepsiburada output, converts ENT-HB barcode values into real stock codes through the database, and produces one Excel workbook with separate sheets for each marketplace.</p></div>
<div class="detail-block wide"><h4>Impact</h4><p>The daily warehouse order-preparation workflow was reduced from repetitive manual Excel work to a single controlled action. Marketplace exports became standardized, barcode-to-SKU conversion was automated, and the final warehouse file became faster to prepare, easier to read, and less prone to human error.</p></div>
</div>
